{"id":11831,"date":"2023-11-10T09:50:03","date_gmt":"2023-11-10T09:50:03","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/the-secret-behind-mona-lisas-smile\/"},"modified":"2023-11-10T09:50:03","modified_gmt":"2023-11-10T09:50:03","slug":"the-secret-behind-mona-lisas-smile","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/en\/the-secret-behind-mona-lisas-smile\/","title":{"rendered":"The secret behind Mona Lisa&#8217;s smile"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><strong>Leonardo da Vinci<\/strong> is undoubtedly one of the greatest geniuses of all time. Although more than 500 years have passed since his death, there is still much to discover in his works. One of his most famous creations is the legendary Mona Lisa. Even though it might seem that it is explored down to the last layer, it is not so, also for the reason that a number of analytical methods belong to invasive or destructive techniques.<\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_11811\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-11811\" style=\"width: 996px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-11811 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2023\/11\/9ead4e34.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"996\" height=\"520\" srcset=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2023\/11\/9ead4e34.png 996w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2023\/11\/9ead4e34-300x157.png 300w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2023\/11\/9ead4e34-768x401.png 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 996px) 100vw, 996px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-11811\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Cultural heritage requires us to use all the detective skills that modern science has to offer during its analysis.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.linkedin.com\/feed\/update\/urn:li:activity:7127638237103169537\/\"><strong>A team of European<\/strong><\/a> scientists managed to obtain an exceptional sample from the bottom layer of the image. This was analyzed using <strong>synchrotron X-ray diffraction<\/strong> and <a href=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/produkt\/ft-ir-mikroskop-raptir-2\/\"><strong>FT-IR microscopy<\/strong><\/a>, which is non-destructive and often it is not even necessary to take a sample from the studied object (also thanks to the large working distance and load capacity of microscope stages, which modern <a href=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/produkt\/ft-ir-mikroskop-raptir-2\/\">FT-IR microscopes<\/a> offer). It was found that it contains a unique blend of high lead saponified oil and cerussite (PbCO<sub>3<\/sub>)-depleted lead white pigment. The most remarkable feature of the sample is the presence of plumbonacrite (Pb<sub>5<\/sub>(CO<sub>3<\/sub>)<sub>3<\/sub>O(OH)<sub>2<\/sub>), a rare compound that is only stable in an alkaline environment.<\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_11813\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-11813\" style=\"width: 800px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-11813 size-large\" src=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2023\/11\/837c272d-839x1024.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"800\" height=\"976\" srcset=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2023\/11\/837c272d-839x1024.png 839w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2023\/11\/837c272d-246x300.png 246w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2023\/11\/837c272d-768x937.png 768w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2023\/11\/837c272d-1259x1536.png 1259w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2023\/11\/837c272d.png 1292w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-11813\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Cross-sectional analysis of a fragment from the Mona Lisa. (A) Optical light microscopy. The white rectangle shows the area mapped by micro-FTIR, while the red rectangle shows the area mapped by SEM\u2212EDS (base maps shown in Figure S5). (B) SEM-BSE map. (C) <a href=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/produkt\/ft-ir-mikroskop-raptir-2\/\">\u03bc-FTIR map<\/a> with NNMA vectors and maps.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>Leonardo probably prepared a thick paint suitable for covering the wooden panel of the Mona Lisa by treating the oil with a high content of lead oxide (PbO). However, his manuscripts draw ambiguous conclusions regarding the use of PbO. Analysis of fragments from The Last Supper confirms that not only PbO was part of Leonardo&#8217;s palette, but also litharge (\u03b1-PbO), massicote (\u03b2-PbO), plumbonacrite and shannonite (Pb<sub>2<\/sub>OCO<sub>3<\/sub>), the latter phase being detected for the first time in a historical image.<\/p>\n<p>It turns out that the <a href=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/produkt\/ft-ir-mikroskop-raptir-2\/\"><strong>FT-IR microscope<\/strong><\/a> is an irreplaceable companion for every adventurer who wants to look under the hands of the old masters.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Leonardo da Vinci is undoubtedly one of the greatest geniuses of all time. Although more than 500 years have passed since his death, there is still much to discover in his works. One of his most famous creations is the legendary Mona Lisa. Even though it might seem that it is explored down to the [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":2,"featured_media":11810,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[125,33],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-11831","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-2023-en","category-news"],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v26.8 - https:\/\/yoast.com\/product\/yoast-seo-wordpress\/ -->\n<title>The secret behind Mona Lisa&#039;s smile - NicoletCZ<\/title>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" \/>\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/en\/the-secret-behind-mona-lisas-smile\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" cont